# apps/web environment (copy to .env.local for local runs; never commit real env files).
# The API base URL, inlined at build time. Every development and preview build uses the DEV API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.quicktestspace.site
# Optional host map "host=zone,..." (zones: public, auth, dashboard, overlay). Unset: the built-in map of the dev
# hosts, the production hosts and *.localhost (apps/web/lib/hosts.ts). Unknown hosts get the public site.
# WEB_HOST_MAP=quicktestspace.site=public,auth.quicktestspace.site=auth,dashboard.quicktestspace.site=dashboard,overlay.quicktestspace.site=overlay
# The marketing website's deployment (github.com/Ankit-KK/hyperchat-frontend), read at build time: the apex
# allow-list in lib/marketing.ts is forwarded to it. An https origin without a path. Required in the production
# deployment (the build fails without it); its URL is not recorded here yet. Unset elsewhere: http://localhost:5174,
# the website's Vite dev server (run it with `npm run dev -- --port 5174` in that repository).
# MARKETING_ORIGIN=https://<the website's production deployment>
